<title>USA: Dodge City feeder steers not well tested- USDA.</title>
<headline>Dodge City feeder steers not well tested- USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>- Feeder steers and heifers 300-600 lbs not enough for a market test, compared with last week, USDA said. Feeder steers and heifers 600-950 lbs $3.00-$6.00 per cwt higher.</p>
<p>Trade very active, demand very good. Receipts 86 percent 600 lbs and over; 06 percent 600 lbs and under; 08 percent cows and bulls with 180 early.</p>
<p>Receipts - 2,151   Last Week - 1,499   Last Year - 3,503</p>
<p>Feeder Steers - (Figures in parentheses are weighted average prices) Medium and Large 1 550-600 lbs 89.00-97.00 (91.03); 32 head 640 lbs 88.00; 650-700 lbs 85.25-90.00 (87.62); 700-750 lbs 82.75-88.00 (86.23); 750-800 lbs 82.25-86.50 (84.55); 800-850 lbs 81.00-85.50 (83.68); 850-900 lbs 80.50-83.65 (82.85); 900-950 lbs 78.75-80.25 (79.97).</p>
<p>Medium and Large 1-2 22 head 702 lbs 77.00; 750-800 lbs 77.75-80.75 (79.51); 11 head 819 lbs 80.60; 850-900 lbs 76.25-80.75 (78.52). Medium 1 750-800 lbs 75.25-82.00 (76.76).</p>
<p>Feeder Heifers Medium and Large 1 600-650 lbs 80.00-87.25 (83.79); 650-700 lbs 80.00-83.00 (80.76); 700-750 lbs 76.50-82.00 (78.96); 750-800 lbs 77.50-80.00 (78.32); 800-850 lbs 75.00-77.00 (75.29). Medium and Large 1-2 600-650 lbs 75.25-79.50 (78.12); 650-700 lbs 75.00- 78.00 (76.51); 800-850 lbs 71.00-72.50 (71.84); 850-900 lbs 71.50-72.00 (71.81).</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
